  "slug": "rhizosphere-meta-omics-5ed4",
  "summary": "Multimodal CRISPR screens, single-cell benchmarks, and ATAC-seq pipelines now resolve context-dependent regulatory effects at population and locus scales.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is functional dissection of noncoding and context-dependent gene regulation using perturbation, reporter, and profiling methods. Several preprints refine CRISPR-based tools: a single-cell benchmark contrasts knockout with interference across 87 sgRNAs targeting 29 unfolded protein response genes, a multimodal study maps overlapping but distinct noncoding elements at the LDLR locus, and Cas9-TurboID proximity labeling profiles protein assemblies at editing sites. Other work addresses measurement context: MPRA variant effects depend on probe position, and PIPPA shows ATAC-seq peak calling performance is dataset-dependent at population scale. A published CRISPR screening review and the OSCAR paired scATAC-seq and scRNA-seq atlas frame these approaches. Breast epigenomic profiling links enhancer-driven variation to genotype across cell types. The novelty lies in pairing multimodal readouts with stringent quality control to resolve regulatory function.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-27"
}
